# Patch 0063 — the Appearance panel: one home for how Kavacha looks, and the
# first place in the product that shows you a colour.
#
# SYMPTOM (user, 2026-08-03): "everything about appearance customization and
# theme is not intuitive. make a new menu just for it in the settings menu, and
# find all theme related settings and put it there ... the color pallete is just
# missing, so please add that in the menu as well."
#
# WHAT WAS THERE. Appearance was spread across five surfaces and none of them
# was the obvious one:
#   * the ⚙ menu's generated Appearance section — nine command rows, the
#     longest section in the menu and the least self-explanatory ("Cycle
#     Interface Density" is a verb where the user wants a choice);
#   * about:preferences#paneKavachaAppearance — theme dropdown, accent picker;
#   * about:preferences#paneKavachaCustomization — layout, in a DIFFERENT pane;
#   * about:studio — theme cards and the CSS editor;
#   * Zen's own Look and Feel pane.
# And nowhere in the menu was there any colour at all. The accent — the control
# people look for first — was two clicks deep in Settings, and themes were a
# list of names you could not see before choosing.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. A sibling <panel> anchored to the same ⚙ button, opened from an
# "Appearance" row pinned under Settings, containing:
#   * Dark / Light / Auto. Kavacha had no such control. Light and dark used to
#     be a side effect of which theme you happened to pick, while Zen's
#     zen.view.window.scheme pref pointed somewhere else entirely; patch 0061
#     made the theme authoritative and this is where you steer it. Auto follows
#     the OS, and choosing a theme by hand ends Auto rather than silently
#     losing to it at the next appearance change.
#   * Theme cards painted from each theme's OWN tokens — five bands: surface,
#     elevated surface, active tab, accent, text. This is "the colour palette is
#     missing", literally. A card is badged when patch 0061's contrast check
#     says the theme cannot be read: the engine repairs such a theme on apply,
#     and silently changing someone's colours without telling them is its own
#     bug.
#   * The accent palette, inline: system + the eight Kavacha swatches + a
#     custom colour. Those eight were a literal array inside ZenWelcome.mjs;
#     they are now one exported constant, because two copies of a palette drift.
#   * Tab style, density, sidebar, as segmented controls over
#     KavachaLayoutEngine.
#   * Everything else the registry holds in the Appearance domain, still
#     GENERATED — so a marketplace component or plugin that registers an
#     appearance command still appears without anyone editing this file. The
#     four commands the panel replaces with a real control are filtered out;
#     they stay registered, so the palette still offers them.
#
# NOT A panelmultiview SUBVIEW: no Kavacha panel uses one, and hide-then-open on
# a shared anchor is the shipped idiom (KavachaWidgetHost.openDashboard).
#
# THREE DEFECTS FIXED IN PASSING, all in surfaces this panel supersedes:
#   * "Use system accent" looked like it did nothing. _renderAccent only
#     assigned the input when the pref matched /^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/, and the
#     reset CLEARS the pref — so the guard failed and the swatch kept showing
#     the colour just cleared. Now resolves the system accent and shows that.
#   * The Settings theme menulist could duplicate entries or go blank.
#     _renderThemes emptied the popup and THEN awaited once per theme, while its
#     own pref observer re-entered it; two runs interleaved remove() and
#     appendChild(). Now resolves first behind a generation guard, swaps once,
#     and reads the active id after the awaits rather than before.
#   * Arc was unreachable outside about:studio. The palette's tab-layout command
#     was a two-way toggle written before patch 0058 and the Customization pane
#     listed two of three options, so an Arc user who touched either was
#     silently dropped to vertical. The command cycles three now and the pane
#     has the third menuitem.
#
# HEIGHT: the panel measures the space below its anchor rather than using vh.
# MEASURED 2026-08-03: inside a XUL popup `100vh` resolves to 808px in a 758px
# window — the popup's viewport is not the window's — so the menu's existing
# `calc(100vh - 10rem)` yields 648px where it means ~598. That is the drift
# patch 0060's D1 note warns about ("re-measure the ANCHOR rather than the
# overhang"). A popupshown correction takes off any residual overhang, so the
# panel-chrome constant is a seed rather than a promise.
#
# WHY NOT A PREF OR AN OVERLAY: the panel is chrome UI built from a system
# module against the command registry and both engines; ui/ and customization/
# reach none of them.
#
# VERIFIED (Marionette, 758px window, buildID 20260803):
#   * Menu at rest: 293px, no scrolling, pinned rows [Settings, Appearance],
#     sections [Navigation, Organization, Productivity, Privacy, Automation] —
#     Appearance no longer among them. Filter "appear" finds the row; arrow keys
#     still walk filter -> Settings -> Appearance (patch 0060 regression pass).
#   * Panel: 360x649 at the shipped three themes, bottom 743 in a 758 window,
#     no scrolling. With a fourth theme installed it scrolls rather than
#     overhanging.
#   * Cards paint the real palettes: Midnight rgb(11,9,18)…, Daylight
#     rgb(247,246,251)…, i.e. the light theme's card is light.
#   * Clicking the Daylight card: kavacha.theme.active -> kavacha-daylight,
#     mode -> light, --kavacha-surface -> #F7F6FB, color-scheme -> light, live.
#   * Clicking an accent swatch: zen.theme.accent-color and --zen-primary-color
#     both -> #4AA3DF.
#   * Layout rows show all three tab styles with the active one pressed.
#
# FILES: src/zen/common/sys/KavachaAppearancePanel.sys.mjs (new);
# src/zen/common/sys/KavachaMenu.sys.mjs;
# src/zen/common/sys/KavachaCommandRegistry.sys.mjs; src/zen/common/moz.build;
# src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-menu.inc.css;
# src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-appearance.js;
# src/browser/components/preferences/kavachaCustomization.inc.xhtml;
# locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl;
# locales/en-US/browser/browser/preferences/zen-preferences.ftl.
# NOTE the two .ftl files: `surfer import` does not copy locales/, so this patch
# needs sync_locales() (build/bootstrap.sh) — i.e. `bootstrap.sh fast` or
# `build`, never the bare `ui` target.
